A page-side throw yields `undefined`. The consumer at :296 asserts `mainRuntime === "undefined" || mainRuntime === false` for "sender authority: a page's MAIN world has no chrome.runtime". So an INSTRUMENT failure is reported as a FAILED SENDER-AUTHORITY CHECK - a security-gate red that reads as a product/security defect. This is exactly the conversion 0lb4 exists to stop, still live in the gate whose composer:false the 0lb4 bead recounts.

